  "question": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2017_che_q41.png\">\r\n\r\nFor same mass of two different ideal gases of molecular weights $M_{1}$ and $M_{2}$, Plots of log $V$ vs log $p$ at a given constant temperature are shown. Identify the correct option.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vQT8G",
      "text": "$M_{1}>M_{2}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "t9TE3",
      "text": "$M_{1}=M_{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6kQQt",
      "text": "$M_{1}    < M_{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rHd1X",
      "text": "Can be predicted only if temperature is known",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For ideal gas, $\\log \\frac{k}{M_{2}}, \\log \\frac{k}{M_{1}}$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2017_che_a41.png\">\r\n\r\n$\\because$\r\n$p V=\\frac{W}{M} R T$\r\nLet, $W R T=K$\r\nTaking log of both the sides of Eq. (i)\r\n$$\r\n\\log p+\\log V=\\log \\frac{K}{M}\r\n$$\r\nor $\\log V=-\\log p+\\log \\frac{K}{M}$\r\n[On compairing Eq. (ii) with $y=m x+C]$ $\\log \\frac{K}{M_{2}}>\\log \\frac{K}{M_{1}}$ or $M_{1}>M_{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
